    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `publish_run` in `app/publish.py`. It creates the dataset repo and uploads `run_dir` to it; all 3 tests pass, including 2 new ones. Nothing was uploaded to the real Hub, so the resume behaviour hasn't been tried against a live repo.\n\n**The dedicated large-folder function is gone in the pinned version.** In the pinned `huggingface-hub==2.0.0`, `upload_large_folder` has been removed. Its job now belongs to `upload_folder`, as long as `hf_xet` is available. With it, `upload_folder` commits a huge folder in several batches to stay under the Hub's limits. If a job dies halfway, running the same call again skips files that are already committed and doesn't re-upload data that's already there. `hf_xet` 1.6.0 is already in `.venv` as a dependency of `huggingface-hub`, so nothing new was added.\n\nWhat `publish_run(run_dir, repo_id, api=None)` does:\n- **Creates the repo:** `create_repo(repo_id, repo_type=\"dataset\", private=True, exist_ok=True)` makes a private dataset repo, or reuses it if it already exists.\n- **Uploads:** `upload_folder` sends `run_dir` to the root of the repo, keeping the folder layout.\n- **Skips files:** it ignores `*.tmp` anywhere in the tree and everything under the top-level `wandb/`.\n- **Takes an optional `api`:** this mirrors `publish_summary` and makes testing easier.\n\n**Behaviour you might not expect:** `publish_run` raises a `RuntimeError` if `hf_xet` is missing or turned off (`HF_HUB_DISABLE_XET`). Without it, `upload_folder` silently falls back to one big commit that can't be resumed, which is exactly the failure you want to avoid. `hf-xet` is only a dependency on x86_64/AMD64 and arm64/aarch64 machines, so this matters if a job ever runs somewhere else.\n\n**Tests added:**\n- One checks the `create_repo` and `upload_folder` calls using a fake API.\n- One runs the ignore patterns through huggingface_hub's own `filter_repo_objects`. It confirms `.tmp` files and `wandb/` are dropped, while a file like `data/wandb.parquet` is kept."
